<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:24Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Deportations on the decline</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9989cda54b05738353d9e8584ff11169fcc999babd24cbf94c76ee96c5b87ca4</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126--231ad2fcde65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a decrease in overall deportations, more people were sent back to Turkey than in previous years. At the same time, Volkswagen is facing a fresh 'Dieselgate' trial. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong sentenced to 10 more years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d90fc83adfdab8bd69a0a8b019714cbde809e9a35d9103c588132171be6521f</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T05:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-sentenced-to-10-more-years/a-79859898--15d97090ad43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-sentenced-to-10-more-years/a-79859898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Joshua Wong, once a teen activist and a poster boy of the "Umbrella Movement," is spending most of his adult life in prison.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Swift space telescope plunges back to Earth in fiery demise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e3e8cd06b24ee6203e10a633629af72f5a22c32d3cbaf826cd8f6dc98a3ea38</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T04:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-swift-space-telescope-plunges-back-to-earth-in-fiery-demise/a-79859805--86b86ba56b3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-swift-space-telescope-plunges-back-to-earth-in-fiery-demise/a-79859805?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">NASA's Swift orbital observatory fell back to Earth after running its mission for more than two decades. A rescue attempt to raise its sinking orbit had earlier failed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats take House and Senate from Republicans in US midterm rout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90d25360cd4f29ecbc36e8d8d31d57f203c6dd4018beeb786d8c673894d99b91</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T23:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/democrats-take-house-and-senate-from-republicans-in-us-midterm-rout/a-79859416--db0c6e2ab972.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/democrats-take-house-and-senate-from-republicans-in-us-midterm-rout/a-79859416?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Democrats will control both chambers of Congress after flipping seats in Republican strongholds across the US in an election seen as a repudiation of President Donald Trump.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bavarian politician Hubert Aiwanger found dead in Berlin hotel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0e0ba670273a486c24c651a26a380144c2eab8c31d22a5cb32ff95035d9f3c7</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115--a5e0e6ba38b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aiwanger was Bavaria's Economy Minister and the chairman of the right-wing populist Free Voters party. The circumstances surrounding his death are still unclear.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Winners, losers, the EU: Five takeaways from the US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ea0e70579fee9674f3b8761af74a4a06d20a79825f78d9e921cd8865baacb55</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901--d5d91689d3d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans suffered a crushing defeat in Tuesday's midterm elections, with the Democrats wresting control of Congress. What does this mean for US politics and the world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>36 years later: Hungary opens Communist-era secret service files</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c339866eae944af84e66bd25319113229fa2ded6dbb5992a16fb91b2ba7f167e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016--dc09772faa12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Decades after the end of Soviet rule, Hungary is releasing all its secret service files. The disclosure is sparking fresh debate about informants, guilt and responsibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Examining viral narratives after the US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e99746ba77360cd35150527ff87270ceaae9e3c551dad0db9b941a9ca3a41c5</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-examining-viral-narratives-after-the-us-midterm-elections/a-79851311--82139c11cec8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-examining-viral-narratives-after-the-us-midterm-elections/a-79851311?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Democrats celebrate major gains, false claims about election fraud have spread. Viral posts alleging illegal voting and election rigging are intended to fuel doubt about the integrity of the vote. DW checks the facts.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>French blood banks targeted by refrigerator cyberattack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d51236fda4a53da2014879de25105dfed0544a32fed5b813a9bc9a57adfd2f20</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-blood-banks-targeted-by-refrigerator-cyberattack/a-79857981--e0b54ca9f23f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-blood-banks-targeted-by-refrigerator-cyberattack/a-79857981?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A cyberattack had attempted to destroy blood plasma by raising the temperatures in cold storage facilities past the boiling point.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The 2011 discovery of neo-Nazi killers aired biases in German policing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:779f5239e3cf34368abad694c076045f268461245553cf620c764df743696c02</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781--949d4ea66003.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many questions still surround the National Socialist Underground whose existence was revealed by neo-Nazi terrorist Beate Zschäpe on November 4, 2011. How has German society reacted to NSU crimes? Has justice been done?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo: Outrage as authorities accused of not helping femicide victim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e11b7b8b0553fd5c5fd716b66600b74e098fd9f91398b457260f58996826ce4d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726--34859fc77a44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite reporting her husband to the police and pleading for protection, Arlinda Zekaj was brutally murdered. Now, thousands in Kosovo are protesting what they say is a dramatic failure of state institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d6c6cca9b73350b26976dcc2902a88ac53a591276cfbcfc765332302ecc1647</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's shifting role in the global drug trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b402d3e94e2327d2769b6f3ae69247e6c469755f020a5554c02cc0c2a2304ed</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720--a33472b9e48a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent discoveries of meth labs suggest parts of Africa are moving beyond drug transit and becoming sites of synthetic drug production.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Potter films turns 25 ahead of new TV series' release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e9f887f2364cb2b926221589e1fd5a4fd8b64c77c547199651f633d8b7bd924</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130--db1dcb8d550c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 2001, "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone" hit cinemas and took the world by storm. Today, anticipation for the new series is high, but its creator, J.K. Rowling, remains a controversial figure.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What the Democrats' midterms win means for the US economy and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c53afe83e0ab9f6c91766d1dc52b36a045836414847557e799ad12e7e15e1a51</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716--124f824b0e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From high oil prices and data centers to tariffs and mounting debt, economic concerns played a key role in the crushing defeat of President Donald Trump's Republicans. So can the Democrats now make a difference?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU says Montenegro on track to become bloc's next member state by 2028</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f9b77ce7442c8bf456163ad8d707fb4d4b4f4ec4c62d5f68e350d3ca9e07ff4</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-says-montenegro-on-track-to-become-bloc-s-next-member-state-by-2028/a-79855011--2c07b9ca6077.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-says-montenegro-on-track-to-become-bloc-s-next-member-state-by-2028/a-79855011?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brussels says Montenegro is likely to become the EU's 28th member state, followed by Albania and Moldova. It said Ukraine needed to speed up reforms and offered fresh hope to Serbia following elections last month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dffa41f33ac437ea376df228b4b05c933b762c2d39dbca839dc90c263589fc90</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Commerce chief hopes for more stable US trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fda54ce3ed7d920e00e9c75c5213238156661fb733f66a625de5c84646524804</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-hopes-for-more-stable-us-trade/live-79854127--6b9f63120529.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-hopes-for-more-stable-us-trade/live-79854127?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German business is pinning its hopes on greater stability in US trade relations after a midterm blow for Donald Trump. Meanwhile, Germany's automakers appear to be feeling less gloomy than in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia deploys troops to Jakarta after wiretapping allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f14af05b1c9caf7798d1faf02bda523c91279f7cefbef3807056fa88658831a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779--6f55d522a605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indonesian troops are being stationed in Jakarta amid wiretapping allegations implicating the president's chief of staff. Suspects are being accused of illegally tapping the president's phones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'largely true' Iran war led to Republican midterm loss</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49bee50c46f225b229ef8262ffba49c24bb09bd84f36e83df7ad1bc7221b2fba</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-says-largely-true-iran-war-led-to-republican-midterm-loss/live-79829440--7f589033d85e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-says-largely-true-iran-war-led-to-republican-midterm-loss/live-79829440?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Democrats won both the House and Senate in a blowout for Republicans, President Donald Trump admitted fuel prices brought on by the Iran war impacted the outcome, but stuck by his decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>BMW reports lower Q3 earnings as China woes mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f6b8c29821560a5cc18a83f5720ce8a6c85e43d0bcf91ad68c06ab5e218e989</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847--9f74c40c2952.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bmw-reports-lower-q3-earnings-as-china-woes-mount/a-79850847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">BMW reports a drop in profits in the July to September quarter amid fierce competition from China.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's celebrated children's author Janosch has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d55e89a31a4a56d05d863e67b285e5da64fbcf496c7d4da16d47285c4c517e1d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600--a3fdc8a2501b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bear, Tiger and Tiger-Duck: The author and illustrator Janosch achieved world fame with his heartwarming children's figures. He died at the age of 95.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>From rotten food to political opponents: Researchers explore how disgust relates to our beliefs, and why the connection is complicated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7790a680108b0d8bae4d64df2b01b7e2c4dd02587b2c8bad71c81b05358e696a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-w/a-79734659--e9b7cd7e436d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-why-the-connection-is-complicated/a-79734659?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some studies have linked disgust sensitivity to socially conservative attitudes. But does disgust shape our politics, or do our beliefs shape what we find disgusting?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How Berlin's Arab queers are building their community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daa5cdf2ddf712739e56c632e74e95f13bf464ccbec397607f43d70e1c43f3be</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143--c676c7f349f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the co-founder of the ADIRA Drag Festival, Lebanese performance artist, drag performer, DJ and cultural organizer Hassandra has become an essential part of Berlin's queer artistic landscape.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Cyprus: From ties with Russia to a strategic alignment with the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89e98e75702d7f32bf926ae7941026510d70b4a9d61d82b8e696fec32283fe55</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251--5a66c266e064.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Republic of Cyprus long balanced ties between Russia and the West. Now, it is phasing out Russian weapons, expanding defense cooperation with the United States and redefining its place in the Eastern Mediterranean.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Multiple flights to European airports targeted by bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75534ff823a02615d28667db9d3424596d817eeb939aa5118f644f6f32250399</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434--863c4364baea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bomb threats involved two passenger planes bound for Warsaw, a Ryanair flight from London to Spain, two flights to Rome and a flight traveling from Israel to the Bulgarian capital, Sofia. No explosives were found.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Football: Spanish player dies on after cardiac arrest on the pitch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7810cd75cc9dee182ce01415fecbf9159d11af6a6f3dc3260dac6f7bb24d738a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398--59e3eb0d85d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-spanish-player-dies-on-after-cardiac-arrest-on-the-pitch/a-79839398?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tenerife forward Jesus de Miguel has died following a collision with the opposing goalkeeper. The Spanish second-division club has said it is "heartbroken" by the loss.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Asian Cup postponed due to Middle East conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34a75cb6f03fbf30656cee190c66f345cddc2857d35621f753a9633101f07ba4</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334--1d2a8af2e01e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/asian-cup-postponed-due-to-middle-east-conflict/a-79837334?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Asian Cup has become the latest sporting event to be affected by the ongoing conflict in the Middle East. Organizers cite "exceptional circumstances" in Saudi Arabia, which has seen several Houthi attacks of late.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Could the AI boom make borrowing more expensive in Europe?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:272659484da9447b5687ee31ff4e8925ac735cca1939ee2cab58cac27eb71c4b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T10:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985--c654959bd451.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-the-ai-boom-make-borrowing-more-expensive-in-europe/a-79511985?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France, Germany and Italy face a volatile bond market as war inflation bites. With US tech giants now issuing billions in AI bonds, they are competing with cash-strapped European governments.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Ukraine in focus at Berlin Security Conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:085e43614130460e6987264ff35fe2c188aa6bcf780faa44a16df3162e4782d0</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T07:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ukraine-in-focus-at-berlin-security-conference/live-79835322--417ad1cade50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-ukraine-in-focus-at-berlin-security-conference/live-79835322?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A security conference in the German capital is addressing defending Europe against threats from Russia. Meanwhile, Germany's justice minister wants to raise penalties for sexual offenses. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey officials considering options after CAS order to reinstate Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0b40eae1988759714be739240cd55bed36112bb3d38af2e6ca0e59b3431a9a8</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451--d3d6cb0a329c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's ruling body is deciding how to respond to a decision by the Court of Arbitration for Sport that allows Russia back into international competition. Germany hasn't ruled out pulling out as a tournament host.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>LA communities kick out Big Oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc504c6dd119218ece23fb018cf5c9c4196334d866f714dd8a14d9112d964281</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843--72df9d2c6283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of advocacy from residents and legal battles with Big Oil, Los Angeles voted to ban drilling and phase out oil extraction in the city. It's the first city in the United States to kick the oil industry out.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Global pedestrian Karl Bushby returns home to UK after 28-year trek</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c234db74eacff502ab7d35fc6163ea3f7cf3181f5dcb59f6e9340f74eae3a4c5</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-pedestrian-karl-bushby-returns-home-to-uk-after-28-year-trek/a-79829564--7ba09cf0439f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-pedestrian-karl-bushby-returns-home-to-uk-after-28-year-trek/a-79829564?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Karl Bushby, a British man who traveled 50,000 km without transport over the past 28 years, has come home. Starting in Chile, he crossed the Americas, Russia and parts of Central Asia and Europe — almost all on foot.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Iliana Yotova won the presidential election in Bulgaria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3aeb7466d6d5439523b5bf1ebdf67ef8d6a44df2ec0d3884a9ee175c4f8fdeb</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T12:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-iliana-yotova-won-the-presidential-election-in-bulgaria/a-79829019--beeabc4abe9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-iliana-yotova-won-the-presidential-election-in-bulgaria/a-79829019?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iliana Yotova won the presidential election in Bulgaria, promising to be a "president of peace." But the campaign showed how divided Bulgarians are about the war in Ukraine and drone attacks in the Black Sea.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Merz says next German president 'must be a woman' — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba485ca3a53aa73bd18d6f1d6e0c8e7818d95332c0ce31cdd930561616e3317d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-says-next-german-president-must-be-a-woman-report/live-79825749--f592c9770ada.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-says-next-german-president-must-be-a-woman-report/live-79825749?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier's second term is due to end in March next year. Meanwhile, Merz has called for 'digital sovereignty' in the era of AI.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Kimi Antonelli makes history as youngest F1 champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c77a05dcf28b24f74d6490c2972eb8608a32b5968ce91d813b79fad5b6c86e96</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T05:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kimi-antonelli-makes-history-as-youngest-f1-champion/a-79825130--6d0086c2458b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kimi-antonelli-makes-history-as-youngest-f1-champion/a-79825130?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kimi Antonelli became Formula One's youngest world champion and Italy's first since 1953 when he finished third in Sunday's thrilling and crash-hit Mexico City Grand Prix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's giant new radar in Kaliningrad raises alarm in NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:564ca2a87240915264be90bf1bad0b995ed957ff862b7e4c1c352b9dfd8486ce</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815--4cdeadba9801.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia is nearing completion of what experts think is a giant radar complex in Kaliningrad, capable of monitoring much of Europe. Experts warn the project could intensify the military standoff between Moscow and NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethnic Germans in Kazakhstan face legacy of the Soviet Union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79241903d448e557b33d31b6e0aceb507147bdc5f76701c4459b3e3e5ffdeb49</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048--09fc50df10b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kazakhstan is struggling to deal with the legacy of the Soviet dictatorship. Some 85 years ago, Stalin deported hundreds of thousands of people: Some 400,000 ethnic Germans living in the USSR were sent to Kazakhstan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's search for a nuclear waste site</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf1ad06af7d08590a895708540d9f96991c3adc2fb3403fb3318d24cb1c9608e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T08:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-search-for-a-nuclear-waste-site/a-79820678--66cee2f12295.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-search-for-a-nuclear-waste-site/a-79820678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland has become the first country with a final storage facility for nuclear waste. Germany is still searching for a site, while some countries have yet to start. Costs are expected to total many billions of euros.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia after Vucic: The winners are losing patience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d0a7bade82ed7a43625f3ce3ad326e5acb7d3bdb82298322282c2b699780380</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T19:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586--7cebe42bf331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the Student List's election victory, Aleksandar Vucic's power apparatus is disintegrating. People want justice as soon as possible. But the losers still hold sway in the judiciary and administration.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Gen Z protests disrupted by violence on Saturday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2a13d87f4674e6fe27af3010d2317e001ae65b22e454f29001a896f23c9b7c1</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694--76fbedb708ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nationwide protests led by young people were largely peaceful throughout the day, but reports about looting and rioting in the evening, especially in Frankfurt, overshadowed the spirit of the demonstrations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Embarrassing name? How we live with names we don't like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be226fd4a0dd8c84970c1cd80d848cadabb8617d5dd3cc68629de4de711a37b4</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T05:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068--afb6ee0b7720.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What happens when your name evokes laughter or ridicule? Research points to negative life outcomes, but some people learn to embrace unfortunate names.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian PM Mark Carney discusses talks with the EU, overdependence on the US and how to deal with Donald Trump in a DW interview.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fe62dbaef40b7a0257fdd5468a610bb3d64cbb7c90ebbb6e98c6437f375b072</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-do/a-79811469--a55bfac7d94c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-donald-trump-in-a-dw-interview/a-79811469?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Mark Carney tells DW that Canada is seeking closer EU ties to "diversify and deepen" partnerships beyond the Americas. Despite German pushback, he said he favors the all-new term "associate membership."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What the rift within the Tsikhanouski family means for the Belarusian opposition in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e0008768f0b700a01fe4f4402d6c6addaaab4fef3eaa142f1c565fcfaafc95d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776--7fdd2527b18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Siarhei Tsikhanouski criticizes the work of his wife, Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, and her office. He also questions her legitimacy. What are the implications for Belarusian political forces in exile?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz hopes for Korean reunification at DMZ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1657f82eb8166ac50f7a5c00a85517f6aec531b7520465d7be676377335ac0da</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T14:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462--f2cebaec800e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-hopes-for-korean-reunification-at-dmz/live-79803462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has expressed hope for Korean reunification during a visit to the heavily fortified border. Meanwhile, President Steinmeier has held talks with China's Xi Jinping in Beijing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b9f2393f67f1d880b27571f1960feda024f7eb6869147151e69e7620017d3a1</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany takes cautious approach on Israeli election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba0ed2294eb50102031aced8ae3f04bac8c055e3687af17d5dab9c3c848a36f2</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184--6eb977f23eb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-takes-cautious-approach-on-israeli-election-results/a-79805184?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German politicians have been slow to respond as they wait to see who is likely to comprise the next coalition. Many are also hoping for a government without religious hardliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>IIHF ordered to allow Russia back into world championships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c27da3d767d3bb53ccda87a5edc96d10e73aa2746622ae784d04f330095a0bac</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650--8e19bd1daa6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iihf-ordered-to-allow-russia-back-into-world-championships/a-79805650?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Court of Arbitration for Sport has ruled that Russian teams must be allowed to take part in international ice hockey tournaments. The IIHF had banned Russia following the country's full-scale invasion of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Many Turkish 'guest workers' hit by poverty in old age</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b11531481bd091c83138884259d30078a52007e9de336a22ac3a1ede62e532e1</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838--0d5019a9af26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/many-turkish-guest-workers-hit-by-poverty-in-old-age/a-79746838?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">West Germany and Turkey signed an agreement allowing the temporary recruitment of workers on October 30, 1961. Sixty-five years on, many so-called 'guest workers' can't live from their pensions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13b937bb4a2d4f2d263aeff82269d103c2dba26f2bf78ddda41e2a8fd58b6e80</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191--0ec0144d606e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Picasso to Andy Warhol, a surprising number of artists have portrayed the German breed. But the dachshund has also at times been co-opted as a political symbol.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Alexander Zverev clinches tennis No. 1 ranking</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4942d178e0f7e12b3438ef380396fea2b54bc51054bb87cf6b2186f0971718cf</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048--1b03a09b61b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-alexander-zverev-clinches-tennis-no-1-ranking/a-79803048?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev is the second German man, after Boris Becker, to clinch the No. 1 spot in tennis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'Star Trek' star Patrick Stewart dies age 86</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1c34a16215bcb33e7e08b398e27f1f6e3098564cf2c2c3e257d44eb30df270</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T22:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/star-trek-star-patrick-stewart-dies-age-86/a-79803071--53b89389ae81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/star-trek-star-patrick-stewart-dies-age-86/a-79803071?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Shakespearean actor landed the role of a lifetime as "Star Trek" Captain Picard. He passed away at age 86.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India increases growth forecast for fiscal year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8460e35d4ea5d41bd70d5a1aff571a6692fca24b708858c78238dac67ca07047</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971--fa1e5ffdabbe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-increases-growth-forecast-for-fiscal-year/a-79798971?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's Ministry of Finance has increased its growth forecasts for the current fiscal year. But it also warned about inflation, particularly for fuel and energy, amid continued instability in the Middle East.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany seeks new head of state</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98ac301b9608495b7e1730e87bd852277225b88362485a3b6640d4879aba2b10</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794--10071c049ea1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-seeks-new-head-of-state/a-79797794?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The question of who should become Germany's new presiden is becoming pressing. Many want to see Germany's first female head of state. Chancellor Friedrich Merz is keeping his cards close to his chest.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Volkswagen logs Q3 operating loss of €5.86 billion on Porsche writedown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11a7dd8b88bd4e850f2d5e7eb233f9022fbbdd3a35f4fea24b7f970ce7d584fd</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-_5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796--74f8be5771cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/volkswagen-logs-q3-operating-loss-of-€5-86-billion-on-porsche-writedown/a-79793796?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Volkswagen Group has filed its worst quarterly performance since the height of the "Dieselgate" scandal in 2015. Share prices climbed in response, however, perhaps because the bad news was so well signposted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia shadow fleet sanctions: Can the EU act without US?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b33b9afba91b5d43fa44ea6b36a2b7b0da5d9899e73a820cbba985d55c7eb00a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T12:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-moves-to-lift-sanctions-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet-could-undermine-western-pressure-on-moscow-and-h/a-79787035--48ad80b5a4bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-shadow-fleet-sanctions-can-the-eu-act-without-us/a-79787035?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is reportedly considering ways to convert "dark tankers" into legitimate vessels, allowing them to transport crude oil that is not subject to sanctions.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Chancellor Friedrich Merz accuses North Korea of threatening Europe's freedom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66348fce713c782995514ef329cf38265fb995d7bfa38041ad8e1b823a03a1ad</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915--91e1e32cf271.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-chancellor-friedrich-merz-accuses-north-korea-of-threatening-europe-s-freedom/live-79792915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Friedrich Merz, who is visiting Seoul, said North Korea is putting Europe's security at risk by sending soldiers to fight for Russia in Ukraine. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European Central Bank (ECB) head Christine Lagarde to step down in February, before her term ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97cb14e5da0577de07e73db1f7738fe89997104a0633c2ab4c4e1796570c1106</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353--c27511a3878b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Central Bank (ECB) President Christine Lagarde is to resign nine months ahead of the end of her 8-year term. European Council President Antonio Costa has said the process to find a successor is underway.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany's health scare highlights the need for better support for elite coaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1d1b2da441ad8faf5a677034d3d1673e461d83b6f8e0648b73c144a746212ba</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-e/a-79764661--fcbaed2aac2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-elite-coaches/a-79764661?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vincent Kompany’s health concern is a reminder that elite football's pressures affect coaches too. Better support, clearer structures and mental health safeguards are increasingly vital.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Evacuation from Oleshky: How are preparations going?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a44c692c020da6876a5a45a0493d3417cbc679afc212d90e2372173176ec658</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001--e77f75613f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A lawyer with the Save Ukraine Foundation, Myroslava Kharchenko, told DW about what has been happening in Russian-occupied Oleshky since a temporary ceasefire brokered by Melania Trump took effect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests in Germany: Is France-style violence looming?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:959e454b2693391d0085d43e70877ac63c9b1269f37fdd452061bcba45168980</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050--fb575275c7ae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-in-germany-is-france-style-violence-looming/a-79788050?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Young people in Germany are preparing to protest over education and climate change. Politicians fear violence like in France, but an expert sees differences.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee7fef3ef55ed0d11d69e03a7284a83ce87123a04fb91902738c07ebf325380</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>EU's 'Made in Europe' push unnerves global auto suppliers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45432750df5b068f2a75a51440f68024718d48b7088c180325bf30155627d030</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579--7391c1bc1a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In shielding Europe's carmakers from Chinese rivals, the EU risks hurting close partners from Turkey and Morocco to Japan and South Korea. Billions in trade and hundreds of thousands of European jobs are at stake.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Russia in Africa: What is Putin hoping to achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aef485c1508eaef102a983d665af2704337939471b2aef002497f9b0c6bdab32</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858--24074440aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its invasion of Ukraine and the resulting rift with the West, Russia has declared that it intends to make a "historic return" to Africa. What have we seen of this so far?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72b1bf1683d52e367061f8c1f23c0ce284859fe7b92a80d858ba7b7b1d6825a4</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478--c3155dbcff43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senegal is hosting Africa's first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian police shoot dead assailant at Israeli Embassy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c79be0819512c13b7743112b2d8ad8a4ab84f7571850573f79d25c4b3a98f5c7</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T08:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905--d152a4aa69fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-police-shoot-dead-assailant-at-israeli-embassy/a-79782905?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A "minor" has been killed by police after attacking a guard at Israel's embassy in Belgrade with knives, the interior minister says. Ivica Dacic said police had declared the highest terror alert after the incident.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:352d2a12cabe25b939c7c6f521c12d497ea8719e8af541e2dec4cab30393d898</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Merz says erosion of global order means middle powers in Europe and Asia must be more assertive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55030bbfe215cbdc58b2a3f61fd0c65bddf6ee86becf8f62f64347fb6433791a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-asse/live-79772992--98272a034e7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-merz-says-erosion-of-global-order-means-middle-powers-in-europe-and-asia-must-be-more-assertive/live-79772992?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During a visit to Singapore, German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said Europe and Germany want to increase free trade with open competition, reliability and a rules-based order.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>England and Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane wins Ballon d'Or</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92de24893868b1ff579a6082d320b11ce680b6842428e2226f1b69f1ab1c9ac8</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/england-and-bayern-munich-striker-harry-kane-wins-ballon-d-or/a-79771067--21e06316b487.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/england-and-bayern-munich-striker-harry-kane-wins-ballon-d-or/a-79771067?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The England captain ends his country's 25-year wait for the prestigious award after scoring 73 goals for club and country last season, beating competition from Lamine Yamal and Kylian Mbappe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What Germany thinks of carmaker Audi's $4 billion deal with Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebafe2957efdeb214767f28c4476ad404b1782d6a4999c685c67d881c8f8b97b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479--6c6f86b95e86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-germany-thinks-of-carmaker-audi-s-4-billion-deal-with-trump/a-79760479?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The luxury carmaker is set to open its first factory in the United States — a move Trump credits to his tariffs. DW examines the German reaction amid a massive auto industry cull at home.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Steinmeier in China: A major state visit in uncertain times</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5a080d6e95d64f3c89763a7bef7b56a8372f063cc15ee671a5a1386a41ad9e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205--23bd9ee47a5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/steinmeier-in-china-a-major-state-visit-in-uncertain-times/a-79764205?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Frank-Walter Steinmeier is traveling to China on a state visit in a period of political and economic uncertainty. Germany is seeking alternative partners in the region but also wants good ties with Beijing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested after nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fefbc86fddbbe2c224f8e00d33ed2a2cf2b718f926877f7d191da5ea3e77ec29</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223--43db314a2270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-after-nationwide-protests/live-79748223?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The French government says more than 1,000 people were arrested following nationwide protests on Saturday. Police and elite security forces were out in force across the country as clashes broke out.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Prague honors Roma resistance fighters against Hitler</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:619e106b9ef3bb682f3901af11a7d2a9f475485d11598c064f58079726c095d0</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T09:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015--c9d68b8992df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/prague-honors-roma-resistance-fighters-against-hitler/a-79725015?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 1,400 Roma fought against the German Nazi occupation in Czechoslovakia. A new exhibition in Prague showcases the stories of partisans and soldiers whose fates barely received any attention for decades.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Bulgaria, record low voter turnout triggers a November 1 presidential run-off in a poll colored by divisions over Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a144365004e2efc6bf495af166c61d1d502d312633f26b9a541d29810537349</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T07:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by/a-79753496--78ae87f6d8b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-bulgaria-record-low-voter-turnout-triggers-a-november-1-presidential-run-off-in-a-poll-colored-by-divisions-over-ukraine-war/a-79753496?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Low voter turnout has triggered a run-off for the Bulgarian presidency. The vote was colored by strong divisions over Russia's war in Ukraine, and Sofia's relations with the Kremlin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey's new deal on Mediterranean maritime boundaries with Libya is exacerbating issues with Greece and the EU</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5b336f7d5867547bf4897660e70bf56d454237f5c5874a7c3247500114cf0f5</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece/a-79745971--8e4f859a6229.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-s-new-deal-on-mediterranean-maritime-boundaries-with-libya-is-exacerbating-issues-with-greece-and-the-eu/a-79745971?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkey and Libya plan to redraw maritime boundaries in the Mediterranean as part of a new economic corridor. This has sparked strong protests from Greece, and has also drawn the European Union into the conflict.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4027f39c77701bf285de416f545548c09447fdcea618ee29bea25b3f114e0186</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's attacks on Ukraine's capital, Kyiv, are intensifying. DW asked people on the ground what life is like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:948a761a4fe512b9abc24bbb6f1cf7a542ba33291593520887f3be6e4cc61816</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T19:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-/a-79741090--9d6ca1b7b337.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-attacks-on-ukraine-s-capital-kyiv-are-intensifying-dw-asked-people-on-the-ground-what-life-is-like/a-79741090?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's attacks on the Ukrainian capital are hitting harder and more frequently, making 2026 one of the long war's bloodiest years for Kyiv. DW asked people on the ground what life is like.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine tries to shut Moscow's airports with drone strikes on Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4322c4cb4b78a618d7046a2d94f46ea1bab98efcfe84207acf609a66d50f565f</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469--16f9cb7db516.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-tries-to-shut-moscow-s-airports-with-drone-strikes-on-russia/a-79737469?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Repeated Ukrainian drone attacks are increasingly disrupting operations at Moscow's airports. The pounding is part of Ukraine's plan to shut down Russia's airpace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sit out FIFA Under-15 World Cup as Russia return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:766ebac1791e6155a1e21f549b5e593d7e411a23432629025c4f104d66c4dd65</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T07:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sit-out-fifa-under-15-world-cup-as-russia-return/a-79734040--d1c93bdcd718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sit-out-fifa-under-15-world-cup-as-russia-return/a-79734040?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany is one a handful of FIFA's 211 nations to refuse an invitation to play at the inaugural Under-15 World Cup. The tournament will also mark Russia's return to the FIFA fold.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Can Germany revive its economy before the far-right AfD gains ground?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b31350cb4f0b2f3e00eeb1b46648314e99ad8c954038f6bb5a840362abc7d5b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T09:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-far-right-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102--ac9492c7777a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-germany-revive-its-economy-before-the-far-right-afd-gains-ground/a-79696102?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflicts, rising costs and Chinese competition are testing Germany's economic model like never before. Can new growth sectors create jobs and ease voters' economic fears, thereby helping contain the far-right AfD?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: AfD's Weidel calls for major EU reforms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebabfbeade1b3226d94d68b7c63845a6addc372274950c59cd306544da0d7b7e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483--29b68ddcd610.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-afd-s-weidel-calls-for-major-eu-reforms/live-79719483?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Far-right Alternative for Germany co-leader Alice Weidel reveals the party's plan to reform the EU. Meanwhile, Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang was in Berlin to talk to developers and investors. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions target Iran's rail sector as Tehran shifts cargo from sea routes to overland corridors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d2124f9419d90abae710accb7dad48acff24928fe1b8064e59c97a92f7c323b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413--6d742d0c6640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-target-iran-s-rail-sector-as-tehran-shifts-cargo-from-sea-routes-to-overland-corridors/a-79681413?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As US sanctions expand to Iran's rail sector, Tehran is relying more heavily on overland links with China and Central Asia. But capacity constraints, delays and costs limit rail's ability to replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Football: German coach Hürzeler flying high in Premier League</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f609553495a8e00679460f399213dd25bfa58fb1ed9a92a9ce1a66f3990e67</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-h_rzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763--701507a044eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/football-german-coach-hürzeler-flying-high-in-premier-league/a-79714763?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fabian Hürzeler is younger than his star player, a fellow Premier League German. But, contrary to his reputation in his homeland, Hürzeler has become a popular figure both on and off the pitch in England.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Rising emissions and temperatures: The cost of Trump's climate retreat is now clear</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28bddb02f7030016a3a21eca9e02921a6f3a1a313425d8d8b8828f29e072f03d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T05:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915--c58ce7a39bf5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rising-emissions-and-temperatures-the-cost-of-trump-s-climate-retreat-is-now-clear/a-79714915?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The world is set to breach the critical 1.5-degree temperature limit, with Donald Trump's US withdrawal from climate action worsening the outlook, according to a UN report. But there is a small silver lining.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Hackers release AfD party emails</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5d60abe5e3a5f28b515f8f4dcf5e1806509a810eecd07ecb76e6007e9ec1438</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-hackers-release-afd-party-emails/live-79709090--0adf9ddcd090.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-hackers-release-afd-party-emails/live-79709090?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD has launched an inquiry after the release of thousands of emails following a cyberattack. Also, investors pledged billions for Germany at a major summit in Berlin. DW has more news from Germany.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ea365779cee27b6a0cfbe566448439168049732c8470d51ca47c718768da6af</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Why US investors are snapping up Germany's famed Mittelstand</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93101d6ff7df6d432efeb7175704e53608ef0cfab003be6ee2ac9867e7f4e81e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421--453454d6f76c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-us-investors-are-snapping-up-germany-s-famed-mittelstand/a-79705421?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Increasing amounts of US capital are flowing into Germany's traditional industrial firms and family-owned businesses. As many business owners struggle to find successors, more companies are becoming acquisition targets.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Brutal, revolutionary empire builder: Genghis Khan's legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:181ca1edd80a7ce82b1a32bb7df6996201743b13dd936d5dce70a45c728ae808</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T08:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112--675146225486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brutal-revolutionary-empire-builder-genghis-khan-s-legacy/a-79697112?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin is host to a major exhibition on the founder of the Mongol Empire and his successors. Here's how Genghis Khan disrupted the course of history.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria seeks suspects in Germany after Starlink sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a770d02b47440aa4d63d6259168ef7dbc0e2003e06314db81a2f07d00dc6222f</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745--e11bc2352fd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-seeks-suspects-in-germany-after-starlink-sabotage/a-79706745?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Bulgarian court has issued arrest warrants for two young German nationals suspected of setting fire to Starlink antennas. The case is reminiscent of another in Poland, which Warsaw says was orchestrated by Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The homeless man living in front of a London mega-mansion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12c8e34596b15c09c1d73ecac977d1ad95be5c2ac80b7359bd11dafc0856ec50</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T10:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-homeless-man-living-in-front-of-a-london-mega-mansion/a-79400925--903398310f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-homeless-man-living-in-front-of-a-london-mega-mansion/a-79400925?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Anders Fernstedt lives in London without any money. The Swedish native has built a most unusual home under the porch of a house worth over €200 million. How did that happen?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d963edd8250af21753546393471dbd385478827df4308249a56c423a7914600</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Who was Eva Mamlok? Berlin square renamed after Jewish anti-fascist resistance fighter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df5f8f960beff9ce8f7456041ece665ef693c998fb39e1ace2f792654a6b733c</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919--fa371a8e7f27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-eva-mamlok-berlin-square-renamed-after-jewish-anti-fascist-resistance-fighter/a-79668919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She started taking action against Hitler as a teenager and never stopped until her death in a concentration camp. Berlin's Blücherplatz is now being renamed after her.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU promotes sovereign, trusted AI as it struggles to catch US and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a51620b4832c30def5c036bb7fb4e8263b897e355927ca92d88b4ac1ef6b7267</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770--286aee32e70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-promotes-sovereign-trusted-ai-as-it-struggles-to-catch-us-and-china/a-79667770?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At an international AI summit in Dublin, EU leaders promoted trusted and independent artificial intelligence. Critics question whether the bloc can close the gap with the US and China while maintaining strict regulation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Formula One in Rwanda: Sportswashing claims vs. hopes for African legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:543b318cf608ba0e336736e6a9c40514a7fadae37105f49311b4870b81162a90</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744--59b33a158fd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-one-in-rwanda-sportswashing-claims-vs-hopes-for-african-legacy/a-79650744?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Formula One will return to Africa for the first time since 1993. There is concern Rwanda are using it as another sportswashing opportunity, but there is also hope the event's legacy can impact wider African society.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>AI-assisted dying? Doris Dörrie's new film addresses prospect of care robots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cda98b266b8cd1431773d05504362f84a2b1480d636ede22406ccea5ee835df3</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-d_rrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715--50ff40522ded.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-dörrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the world debates the dangers of artificial intelligence, filmmaker Doris Dörrie explores how humanoid robots could change the way we deal with aging, caregiving and how people choose to die.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's elections matter for the planet. This is why</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a99106cb01fa77039c900a0ddebb712cf8d17c8cf8d3ea2289551256ede9c0f</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T09:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-elections-matter-for-the-planet-this-is-why/a-79659928--00329e582e5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-s-elections-matter-for-the-planet-this-is-why/a-79659928?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazil is heading back to the polls, but the impact could be felt worldwide. With the Amazon vital to the health of the planet, the election could help shape its future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Chinese tech brands are outpacing Western rivals from EVs to robot vacuums</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29e05303df9ff2ffa9eece5df0fa914cf5617ea31dec1cddf16fba068d8f6825</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-chinese-tech-brands-are-outpacing-western-rivals-from-evs-to-robot-vacuums/a-79646187--a8751d31a3ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-chinese-tech-brands-are-outpacing-western-rivals-from-evs-to-robot-vacuums/a-79646187?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From action cameras and smartphones to EVs and robot vacuums, Chinese brands are gaining ground worldwide, despite privacy and security concerns. What's driving their rise, and can European rivals keep up?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City, the UAE and the UK's PM in a political tangle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6892076a95d36151bdcdbd88d15e7dde52dcc59ec3e4d128d12b8954b1eddbc</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T08:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-pm-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729--9d27bb4511dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-the-uae-and-the-uk-s-pm-in-a-political-tangle/a-79664729?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly 20 years after arriving in England, Manchester City's UAE owners could exit amid cheating charges. That would pose a challenge for a city — and prime minister — closely tied to Abu Dhabi.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's diesel deal with Russia is unlikely to significantly lower global fuel prices despite expectations of rapid relief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95eb0503e3dd0c09dee01b206ba8d84e55712ebdcd31aacc74c41069e990b733</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expect/a-79659601--8934faa2519e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-s-diesel-deal-with-russia-is-unlikely-to-significantly-lower-global-fuel-prices-despite-expectations-of-rapid-relief/a-79659601?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the world's largest diesel exporter, the US benefits from high prices. At home, however, consumers are feeling the strain of rising living costs. Why Donald Trump's deal with Russia is unlikely to change that.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>FIFPRO report highlights growing pains in women's football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bca6c044a1016699073dd0632ae21eaacaec02de7ea2c2233a7f7462e659768</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T08:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013--365fa34aee7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifpro-report-highlights-growing-pains-in-women-s-football/a-79648013?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Expected global revenue of over $1 billion and new faces at the U17 World Cup show women's football is booming, but a recent report also highlights need for better structures globally.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden treasure in discarded wearable and fast tech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:619febc60d9a7a1bdbc0c9207fe52a88115151921b89bd7976a4cf3cbebff4cf</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611--7010f2eed048.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-treasure-in-discarded-wearable-and-fast-tech/a-79649611?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sales of fast tech like mini fans and disposable e-vapes, as well as wearable health tech such as heart monitors and smartwatches are soaring. They're creating a new e-waste problem but are full of hidden treasure.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Formula 1: Rwanda to bring sport back to Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa6fbe6e64623b326e5cdf942b58a17c1e140ce2b807340091c9416252da107d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217--ee284b399c6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/formula-1-rwanda-to-bring-sport-back-to-africa/a-79649217?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The last time Formula 1 hosted a race in Africa was way back in 1993. But a new track in Rwanda is set to host a Grand Prix in "the early 2030s," continuing the country’s investment in international sport.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's China calculation shifts as import pressures eclipse export benefits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c915a5261b9398990b6f01b837f2131ee85ff52fe1598951dbdd0dace144b8a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852--c4df7eb8a062.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-china-calculation-shifts-as-import-pressures-eclipse-export-benefits/a-79571852?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has long resisted tougher action against China, fearing retaliation. But rising pressure on key industries has pushed Berlin to seek stronger EU trade-defense powers to protect its industrial base.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>125 years of Thomas Mann's 'Buddenbrooks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fd94d916fc60b81f9aaac5b55ffc3fc73a20b40aca6cdf4bcb1a93b7e8950c2</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T08:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236--20da98f1ab2b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/125-years-of-thomas-mann-s-buddenbrooks/a-44107236?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This over 1,000-page masterpiece offers a panoramic view of society in the 19th century and exposes the collapse of a merchant family: unrecognized sons, disillusioned daughters and the loss of middle-class ideals.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Pope lung nodule: Could it be cancer?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f49e5a900afcb12e8d6b9ebe846470f6800d0622c95a42781d5bbb57ad5aba9c</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503--9cf198017761.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-lung-nodule-could-it-be-cancer/a-79641503?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The case of Pope Leo shows how small lung nodules are often found during routine health checks. Quick treatment is generally advised before nodules can grow to become larger life-threatening masses.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's women: Ena Mahmutovic makes her case to become Germany's next No.1 goalkeeper</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28923f0ebe181b5b98e2a8cabef1582cc6e51cd3bcf5cce19d0aa0dff14be2a8</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T09:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341--71931b21638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-women-ena-mahmutovic-makes-her-case-to-become-germany-s-next-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79609341?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's win against Australia saw Ena Mahmutovic excel in goal. The 22-year-old Bayern Munich goalkeeper is considered the successor to Ann-Katrin Berger and is making a name for herself.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How green is Europe's urban public transport? A data-driven reality check</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8b031beb9d4bea7863c331e494ad4929d579ff6b8a91037de4efd76692a7fdf</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721--a78a7db30bc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-green-is-europe-s-urban-public-transport-a-data-driven-reality-check/a-79406721?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greener buses and cleaner fleets are reshaping public transport across Europe. But are cities moving fast enough to meet their zero-emission goals?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>UK students call for school uniforms to be banned in pornography</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2163e52487e54d226201e786773d1769e3706b07b8de93eeeb1ae9b176e105b1</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T07:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324--e21f080b6070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-students-call-for-school-uniforms-to-be-banned-in-pornography/a-79554324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Short skirts, knee-high socks, white blouses: Girls' school uniform items are widely used as costumes in pornographic videos. As students experience harassment, a group wants to change that.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ebd61ed0eb9b13e2e1fb3a27d458a30b28af5ba3b24191c7c16ed89004e68c</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af4ab47e711a9ae96f95fb95f26329ca2e3eb5b195a2c5bd26be0fdc7554dfa4</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9fe52a4a24015d6bda7630994a681f873021adfdcc2372ffdf5dd655df2314b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ac4e7541e59dbe32e0b7e61bae89a431b2fd0c