.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The works of this year's Nobel Prize-winning poet and essayist Anne Carson can feel slightly daunting. Here are some keys to understanding her universe.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Early-onset cancer rising worldwide: Causes, risk, prevention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cddf3b807fc7079b33188c143796d77c4ca2e82e2313433a39a603c4853d7d0d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097--5416293e8076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Across Latin America, early-onset cancer rates have risen, especially of bowel, breast and cervical cancers. But it is a worldwide trend.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>How a multibillion-dollar oilfield has ignited the UK-Argentina feud over the Falklands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b087cdb11b328d186450e40f134ed5db11d9e7f07e746a4de2aebcbb80714335</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973--b9ae4084dbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentina and the UK once fought a war over the Falkland Islands. Now, the multibillion-dollar Sea Lion oil project has reignited old tensions, with Buenos Aires seeking to put a stop to the plans.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature goes to Canada's Anne Carson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a68eada5e0e63a4ef60882f98af7642632c3d449c07bf79b6717bee4176fd5f2</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136--7b591c2af8dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Carson won for her "bold and inventive oeuvre." The decorated poet and essayist is known for her reverence for Latin and Greek classics.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>'90s art scene in the UK: An international, edgy trendsetter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:afeaccc778e15454eaa81138619b1c683f871fd5bdc2d8632f91eec3704b031d</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777--d9e1246b3502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 1990s are remembered for Brit-pop and provocative fashion, but beyond the nostalgia, it was a decade of cultural experimentation and social change. Tate Britain's new exhibition looks past the familiar icons.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in chemistry goes to Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6930d0678d1b404a8a603a7665a9f7088339404f7b0a2126e394a34ba323107</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924--1eccf7a6b469.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-chemistry-goes-to-henri-b-kagan-and-kenso-soai/a-79573924?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai won the Nobel Prize in chemistry for their groundbreaking discoveries related to the origin of chirality and life's building blocks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20169ef4795d464d9601c45890d76b18bfbae8434e1ce50a62b886a131ac60ba</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ronaldo stays on under cloud as Messi exits internationals</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:541453a73e2aa5337d25ec1c322906c4758970a79a13b8879d64b6ba54f07399</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551--518c4a71824f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ronaldo-stays-on-under-cloud-as-messi-exits-internationals/a-79574551?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Just hours before Lionel Messi played his last match for Argentina, Cristiano Ronaldo posted his latest salvo in a row with Portugal. Ronaldo wants to play on despite the troubles, while Messi bathed in adulation.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nobelitis — How winning a Nobel Prize can give you delusions of grandeur</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4f3265b608d51a6a55d07e88ad117f8f8d7b0b7cae36286fa96f05f4ab919</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772--1ee420badedc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobelitis-how-winning-a-nobel-prize-can-give-you-delusions-of-grandeur/a-79525772?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After being chosen for one of the world's most prestigious awards, some Nobel laureates lose touch with reality and suddenly start spouting unscientific nonsense. They're afflicted by what some have called "Nobelitis."</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Emerging economies are embracing solar power and skipping fossil fuels much faster than Europe or the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1fc38297532a7978aceeb1d4b27703dc858bfea58683b755693a131631924db</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-th/a-79474847--a24cf177c41d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/emerging-economies-are-embracing-solar-power-and-skipping-fossil-fuels-much-faster-than-europe-or-the-us/a-79474847?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Renewable electricity is cheaper than ever. While the West got rich on coal and oil, some of the world's poorest countries are banking on solar, wind and water instead.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
